  "finalText": "I triaged T-1041 and checked the ticket afterwards to confirm the changes. It is now **sev3**, due **2026-03-17T17:20:00Z**, assigned to **E-301 Yuki Sato**, and its status moved from new to open.\n\n- **Severity:** The ticket is for the VPN service and affects one team. The escalation matrix rates VPN with team impact as sev3. About nine people on the Berlin sales floor can't connect, so team impact fits.\n- **Deadline:** The ticket had no deadline. I triaged it at 2026-03-17T09:20:00Z by the service desk clock, and sev3 has a 480-minute response target. 09:20Z plus 8 hours gives 17:20Z.\n- **Assignee:** The network-primary rotation owns the VPN service. At the 17:20Z deadline, its on-call engineer is E-301 Yuki Sato, whose shift runs from 08:00Z to 20:00Z. The deadline is well inside that shift, so there's no handover to worry about.\n\nThe ticket didn't ask for a particular severity or engineer, so nothing conflicted with the rules. I made no other changes and touched no other ticket.",
